        "original_id": "b61093c3-b9c5-5047-ba32-90d8ba7cf269",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kathy Mattea, Don Williams, Richard Leigh\n- Products: “Come from the Heart”, Willow in the Wind, Traces, Old Friends\n- Topics: Don Williams discography, Kathy Mattea discography, Billboard Hot Country Singles & Tracks\n\nFacts:\n- Don Williams first recorded and released “Come from the Heart” on his 1987 album Traces.\n- Richard Leigh released “Come from the Heart” in 1988 on his album Old Friends.\n- Kathy Mattea released “Come from the Heart” as a 1989 single in conjunction with her album Willow in the Wind.\n- Kathy Mattea’s 1989 single “Come from the Heart” became the version most known.\n- Don Williams is an American country music artist, and the Don Williams discography is a detailed discography for him.\n- Kathy Mattea had four Top 10 singles that reached #1 on the Billboard Hot Country Singles & Tracks chart: “Goin' Gone,” “Eighteen Wheels and a Dozen Roses,” “Come from the Heart,” and “Burnin' Old Memories.”",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
